    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d521">

                <pb facs="0463" n="347" xml:id="pg347"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Smith to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams–Extracts.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 20, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Because of seriousness of revolution in north, President Zamor will go to the
                    front tomorrow.* * * In the absence of the President the Government will be in
                    the hands of a Commission to be created tonight and which will act in
                    conjunction with the Cabinet. Port au Prince is quiet but the presence of a
                    naval vessel appears to be of the utmost importance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
